# Feral Encounter: "Look at the top five cards of your library. You may exile a creature card from among them. Put the rest on the
# bottom of your library in a random order. You may cast the exiled card this turn. At the beginning of the next combat phase this
# turn, target creature you control deals damage equal to its power to up to one target creature you don't control." Bot1's top five
# are Lightning Bolt, Llanowar Elves, Island, Mesa Pegasus and Island: it exiles the Elves (a creature card, only one of the two
# the five hold) and the other four go to the bottom, the sixth card staying on top. The Elves, cast from exile for {G}, are the
# only card cast this way: the turn's Bolt is not in exile. No target was chosen on the cast; at the beginning of combat Bot1
# chooses its Grizzly Bears (2/2) and Bot2's Grizzly Bears (2/2): the damage is dealt by Bot1's Bears alone and equal to its power
# (CR 120.3), so Bot2's Bears dies and Bot1's takes none. Bot2's Bears is refused as the creature you control and
# Bot1's Elves as the one you don't.

